# JVM options for the connector and the admin commands, on a host or in a container (design §7.5, §14.1, §14.3).
# Read with java @<this file>. They follow JDK_JAVA_OPTIONS and JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS on the command line, so those can
# add tuning but not undo these. Container-only options are in container/container.options.

# PHI hygiene: no heap dumps, core dumps or crash logs (hs_err files hold raw memory near the crash), and no attach
# (jcmd could otherwise take a heap dump).
-XX:-HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-CreateCoredumpOnCrash
-XX:ErrorFile=/dev/null
-XX:+DisableAttachMechanism
# Exit on OutOfMemoryError so the orchestrator or service manager restarts a clean process.
-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError
# No hsperfdata file in the temporary directory.
-XX:-UsePerfData
# Java 25 otherwise warns when libraries load native code.
--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED
